[2026-01-30T14:36:50.572Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Implementation: Consolidate duplicated theme color mappings into centralized theming utility system\n\n## Context Area\nReport Viewing System\n\n## Description\nConsolidate duplicated theme color mappings into centralized theming utility system\n\n## Implementation Details\n\n## Vision\n\nConsolidate the duplicated theme-aware color mapping logic into a centralized theming utility system that provides consistent color palettes across all badge, card, and visualization components.\n\n## Business Value\n\n- Reduces code duplication across 10+ components that define identical light/dark color mappings\n- Single source of truth for color consistency when theme requirements change\n- Faster development of new themed components with pre-built utilities\n- Easier A/B testing of color schemes without touching multiple files\n\n## Scope\n\n**Included:**\n- Extract badge color configurations (TypeBadge, SourceTypeBadge, PriorityBadge, StatusBadge)\n- Consolidate card background/border color mappings\n- Create theme-aware utility hooks and classes\n- Migrate existing components to use the new system\n\n**Out of scope:**\n- Changing the visual design of any component\n- Adding new themes beyond radar/swiss\n- Modifying the ThemeContext provider itself\n\n## Key Components\n\n1. `shared/themeColors.ts` - Centralized color palette definitions for both themes\n2. `useThemedColors` hook - Returns appropriate colors based on current theme\n3. Updated badge components using the centralized system\n4. Updated card components using the centralized system\n\n## Technical Approach\n\n1. Audit all files for repeated theme color patterns (lightColors/darkColors objects)\n2. Create comprehensive color palette type in `themeColors.ts`\n3. Build `useThemedColors(category)` hook that returns appropriate palette\n4. Create Tailwind-compatible class generators\n5. Migrate components one category at a time (badges first, then cards)\n6. Remove duplicate color definitions from individual components\n\n## Files to Modify\n\n- `src/components/report/shared/themeColors.ts` - NEW: Central color definitions\n- `src/components/report/shared/Badges.tsx` - Remove inline colors, use centralized\n- `src/components/report/shared/Cards.tsx` - Remove inline colors, use centralized\n- `src/components/report/tabs/EntitiesTab.tsx` - EntityTypeCard uses inline colors\n- `src/components/report/tabs/PerspectivesTab.tsx` - perspectiveColors object\n- `src/components/report/views/AnalysisView.tsx` - priorityColors inline definition\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n- [ ] No component defines its own lightColors/darkColors mapping\n- [ ] All badge components use shared color utility\n- [ ] Theme color changes can be made in single file\n- [ ] Type safety for color palette access\n- [ ] No visual regression in either theme\n\n## Potential Challenges\n\n- Component-specific color needs may not fit generic palette (mitigation: allow component-level overrides)\n- Tailwind class purging with dynamic class generation (mitigation: use safelist or static class references)\n\n## Instructions\n\n1. Read and understand the implementation details above\n2. Identify all files that need to be modified\n3. Implement the changes following the guidance provided\n4. Ensure code quality and type safety\n5. Test the changes work as expected\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an accepted Development Direction.\nFocus on implementing exactly what is described above.\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"063d9692-0974-4418-8890-3933b0ef315a","uuid":"b0d5d8b3-c312-4f91-9e74-2b0f56e2b774","isSynthetic":true}
